Line 2: I expected "," here, but found "which".
        a name which is text.
               ^^^^^
Write each field like "a name, which is text.".

Line 3: Something is missing after "plus".
        an age, which is a number, starting at 0 plus.
                                                 ^^^^
Add a value there, like a number, some text in quotes, or a name.

Line 4: A list can't be "or nothing".
        a size, which is a list of numbers or nothing.
                                           ^^^^^^^^^^
To say there's nothing in it, use an empty one, like "an empty list of numbers".

Line 5: I expected "which is" here, but found "is".
        a weight, is a number.
                  ^^
Write it like "a name, which is text.".

Line 6: I expected the field to end after "text".
        a color, which is text and more.
                               ^^^
Write one field per sentence, like "a name, which is text.".

Line 7: This line is indented more than the fields above it.
            a tail, which is text.
    ^^^^^^^^
Line the fields up with each other.

Line 10: Something is missing after "is a kind of thing".
    a cat is a kind of thing
          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Write it like "a dog is a kind of thing with:".

Line 11: I expected ":" here, but found the end of the line.
    a bird is a kind of thing with
                                  ^
Write it like "a dog is a kind of thing with:", with its fields indented below.

Line 12: The fields of "fish" go on the lines below, indented.
    a fish is a kind of thing with: a fin, which is text.
                                      ^^^
Write each one on its own line, like "    a name, which is text.".

Line 14: A method is for a kind of record, but this is a number.
    to bark, for a number:
                   ^^^^^^
Write the kind of record it works on, like "to bark, for a dog:".

Line 16: I expected ":" or "with" here, but found "loudly".
    to wag, for a dog loudly:
                      ^^^^^^
Write it like "to rename, for a dog, with new name:".

Line 19: I expected the name of a field here, but found "3".
    let rex be a new dog with name "Rex" and 3.
                                             ^
Give each field's name and then its value, like "a new dog with name "Rex" and age 3".

Line 20: A new record inside another one needs parentheses.
    let rex2 be a new dog with name "Rex" and friend a new dog with name "Fido" and age 2.
                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Otherwise it isn't clear which one the fields after it belong to. Write it like "(a new dog with name "Fido" and age 2)".

Line 21: "let" makes a new name, so it can't change a field.
    let rex's age be 4.
           ^^
To change a field, write "set rex's ... to ...".

Line 22: Something is missing after "'s".
    say rex's.
           ^^
Write the name of a field after it, like "rex's name".

Line 23: I expected a name or a field here, like "rex's name".
    set (rex) to 5.
        ^
A value in parentheses can only be changed through one of its fields, like "(item 1 of dogs)'s name".

Line 24: Something is missing after "with".
    let tail be a new dog with.
                          ^^^^
Give each field's name and then its value, like "a new dog with name "Rex" and age 3".
